ister's spouse  or the lack of well she she has had  formal support  she has had a 100 000 pound a year  director of communications paid for  based in downing street to give her  advice as an extraordinary situation to  be in  i don't believe that dennis thatcher  ever benefited from any  such munificence in recent decades in  fact throughout history  the spouses of prime ministers in the  united kingdom have actually  tried to audition to show they do not  have influence  dennis thatcher as you referred to very  successfully portrayed himself as a sort  of silly old buffoon  precisely to go under the radar in this  way sherry blair who is of course an  extremely distinguished and successful  barrister in her own right  was constantly having to demonstrate  during her husband's time in downing  street  that she was not mixing up her  professional and her personal life  and i suggest that is quite as it should  be  we do not have first ladies or first  gentlemen we have not had first  girlfriends before  and it is very desirable for our country  that that remains the case  and kate andrews perhaps britain then is  the model that america should follow and  not  vice versa well douglas is completely  right to point to the tension that the  role has created historically in the  united states  when george washington's wife martha  washington was first dubbed lady  washington  people felt very uncomfortable about  this it it rank of nobility and that was  exactly what america had just  fought to get itself rid of  so the title itself has actually been  contentious uh really going back  all the way in american history but i  would argue that perhaps it's the best  of a bunch of bad options because  in reality i think it's true certainly  true in america but  becoming increasingly true in the uk you  have to have something to do  if you are in one of these positions we  no longer live in a society  where women are just automatically going  to do the domestic job  um and in 